# Decision 0066 — Activate Schema V2 and Adopt the Decision-0019 Successor

Status: ACTIVE — SCHEMA V2 ACTIVATED

## Authority

This activation is executed under Decision 0065:

`documentation/decisions/0065-authorize-explicit-schema-v2-activation-execution.md`

Decision-0065 authorization commit:

`aa4b85e74f56adab581faf379a09ee69ce1ec30f`

## Schema V2 activation

Schema V2 at:

`config/schemas/protocol_specification.v2.schema.json`

with SHA-256:

`c6ebb5ef2214c4168283f9009d1f7ce6e88d2ff928853fe6a57ed1f7521c6956`

is active for canonical protocol specifications whose declared
`schema_version` dispatches to Schema V2.

The Schema V2 file itself is not modified by this activation.

## Active Schema V2 hash contract

The exact reviewed active form:

`evidence/annotation_preparation/protocol_specification_schema_successor_v2/schema_v2_hash_contract_finalization_package_v1/02_active_form_v2_hash_contract.REVIEW_CANDIDATE.json`

SHA-256:

`37f035bb617f5598a0e368ba3b60b4bf1e69e4e69ce2f1053d71c0fcc96619e9`

is installed byte-for-byte at:

`config/protocol_content_hash_canonicalization.v2.json`

No transformation is applied.

## Active schema-version dispatch

The exact reviewed active form:

`evidence/annotation_preparation/protocol_specification_schema_successor_v2/schema_v2_activation_artifact_finalization_package_v1/02_active_form_version_dispatch.REVIEW_CANDIDATE.json`

SHA-256:

`67a96c3eda8de95fa6c55342d5d33ea725e16cea8af21fcb4f3b8945b9d4eeee`

is installed byte-for-byte at:

`config/protocol_specification_schema_version_dispatch.v1.json`

No transformation is applied.

The version-dispatch policy therefore governs schema-version selection at the
canonical protocol-specification boundary.

## Adoption of the Decision-0019 successor

By this explicit activation decision, the reviewed successor active form:

`evidence/annotation_preparation/protocol_specification_schema_successor_v2/schema_v2_activation_artifact_finalization_package_v1/05_active_form_decision_0019_successor.REVIEW_CANDIDATE.md`

SHA-256:

`a96f9d8b6811a9f9170a18de9ff8be6f80a3704b9e6a13c59fbb88e423bec3bb`

is adopted by exact SHA-256-bound reference and is operative for
version-dispatched canonical protocol specifications from this activation
commit onward.

Historical Decision 0019 remains byte-immutable and continues to serve as the
historical V1 governance record.

## Existing V1 artifacts

This activation does not migrate or rewrite existing V1 canonical artifacts.

The following remain byte-unchanged:

- `config/protocol_content_hash_canonicalization.v1.json`
- `documentation/decisions/0019-canonical-library-protocol-specification-path-convention.md`
- `config/protocol_specifications/zlib.json`
- `config/protocol_specifications/libpcap.json`

## Explicit non-authorizations

This activation does not:

- define a positive V4-to-V2 mapping;
- authorize a positive V4-to-V2 mapping;
- create `config/protocol_specifications/curl.json`;
- authorize analyzer implementation;
- authorize analyzer execution;
- authorize baseline execution; or
- authorize repair.

## Next boundary

Any positive V4-to-V2 mapping remains a separate governance action and must be
independently justified and authorized before `curl.json` can be created.
